  "notes": "⛔ **Mode A only.** The research gives two lanes and then tells the generator to pick one: the Houston 1991–2002 played-band model, or the 2010-onward pad-and-mix model. This entry is Mode A — busy melodic bass, real chord motion, kick and snare dominant — and the cinematic-trap synth lane (CS-80, Jupiter-8, Oberheim, polyphonic aftertouch, sustained beds over someone else's drums) is deliberately NOT modelled here, because a model spanning both is neither. The bass is the signature and it is quoted: \"all my bass parts are like old Cream; Jack Bruce\", meaning busy, melodic, fill-heavy rather than a root pedal. That is the lowest `followRootsProb` in this batch by a distance, the widest bass register, five passing tones and the highest `anticipationProb` — a bass that leads rather than follows, which is why ⛔ `drums.bass808.role` moves off `bassline` and the `bassline` block becomes a real part. `counter_riff` is the engine's only other 808 role and is a near-fit rather than a description; the sub is tuned and gated the way he learned it from Marley Marl and holds still under the played line. The mix philosophy is authored as balance: \"it's all about kick, snare, and vocals; everything else is just extra bullshit\", so `velocityTiers.accent` and `main` sit at the top of this batch while `percs.gainOffsetDb` and the hat velocities sit at the bottom. Harmony is his own playing — 4-bar progressions with real motion, rock/blues-informed minor — with sustained pads under the loop and guitars treated with echo, which is the `spacey_keys` timbre and the legato articulation. Sections change by instrument entry, so `transitions.fillBeforeSection` is false and the outros are long. ⚠ `high`, matching the research: the gear, the 808 practice, the bass idiom and the mix philosophy are directly sourced. The tempo numbers are the LOW-CONF part, and the 68–80 half-time screw-adjacent band is not modelled. Perc lanes and chord family weights are INFERRED. ⚠ `fills.snareRollLadder` is off — with both fill periods at 4 bars the big fill wins and the inherited climbing ladder reads no seed, so it would write one identical fill on all 200. ⚠ **`lockTo808` raised from 0.3 to 0.47.** The 808 takes each kick with this probability, and at 0.3 over this model's 12-kick floor a seed could produce no 808 at all — which `bass808.rs` refuses, because a declared 808 that sometimes vanishes is a part a producer cannot rely on. It is still well under a lock: a good share of kicks carry no sub. ⚠ The bass ceiling came down from 50 to 49 so it stays under a chord part that starts at 50 — `coherence.rs` requires the highest bass note to sit at or below the lowest chord note, and this model overlapped by 1.",
